WEBVTT

00:12.554 --> 00:15.682
Urine tests were conducted
in schools nationwide

00:15.765 --> 00:17.600
under the ERPB's direction.

00:17.684 --> 00:21.479
The ERPB stated the tests were intended
to detect and treat at an early stage

00:21.563 --> 00:25.275
kidney abnormalities and diabetes-related
conditions among students.

00:25.358 --> 00:27.110
While some are questioning

00:27.193 --> 00:31.031
whether the tests are meant
to detect drug activity in schools,

00:31.114 --> 00:34.993
several schools have refused to take part,
citing final examinations.

00:35.994 --> 00:38.329
This is Seungyeon High School,

00:38.413 --> 00:41.958
known as the most academically competitive
school in Gangnam.

00:42.042 --> 00:45.336
It also sends the most students
to SNU Medical School nationwide.

00:45.420 --> 00:47.505
You must know it well from living there.

00:48.089 --> 00:50.091
My mom wanted me to go to this school,

00:50.175 --> 00:52.927
so my family moved nearby
when I was seven.

00:53.011 --> 00:54.512
Weren't you at a science school?

00:57.307 --> 01:03.146
Seungyeon High School is known
for having very pushy parents.

01:03.646 --> 01:06.900
CLASS S

01:09.903 --> 01:12.405
This is the last exam
that counts for early admission.

01:12.906 --> 01:15.325
If you blow this,
the CSAT is your only option.

01:15.408 --> 01:17.869
Unless you want that, do well today.

01:17.952 --> 01:19.037
Yes, sir.

01:19.120 --> 01:20.663
Okay, let's get started.

01:42.102 --> 01:44.521
Is it Class 1, Class 2, and then Class S?

01:45.105 --> 01:48.817
I told you this school sends
the most students to med school in Seoul.

01:48.900 --> 01:52.987
This is a special class
for those aiming for med school.

01:53.613 --> 01:57.575
It's basically a class
of the school's top students.

02:33.903 --> 02:35.530
My boy!

02:37.282 --> 02:39.784
Congratulations
on getting into SNU Medical School!

02:39.868 --> 02:41.494
-My son!
-Congratulations!

02:41.578 --> 02:42.704
This is huge!

02:43.288 --> 02:44.247
Congrats!

02:49.836 --> 02:50.837
Congrats!

02:54.549 --> 02:56.092
Hyeon-min, congrats!

03:12.108 --> 03:13.067
Who are you?

03:13.151 --> 03:15.486
-We're from the ERPB.
-Hey, are you okay?

03:30.835 --> 03:32.170
His nose is bleeding.

03:32.253 --> 03:34.422
-Let's take him to the nurse's office.
-Okay.

03:35.340 --> 03:36.591
-Here.
-Let's get you up.

03:36.674 --> 03:38.426
Sir, where is the nurse's office?

03:38.509 --> 03:40.720
-Turn left, then go down.
-Left? Okay, thank you.

03:54.817 --> 03:55.818
-Here.
-Be careful.

03:55.902 --> 03:57.570
-Hold his head from the back.
-Okay.

04:08.373 --> 04:09.207
URINE TEST CHECKLIST

04:09.290 --> 04:10.208
Class 6…

04:10.291 --> 04:12.418
Stop the exam right now!

04:13.002 --> 04:14.963
My kid can't finish the exam!

04:18.508 --> 04:20.927
Do you want to see
my son and me die here today?

04:21.511 --> 04:23.888
Will you take responsibility
if he doesn't get in?

04:23.972 --> 04:26.182
Hyeon-min will take the exam
no matter what!

04:29.852 --> 04:31.479
-Jung Hyeon-min!
-Ma'am.

04:31.562 --> 04:33.523
He passed out in the middle of the exam.

04:34.941 --> 04:36.484
How much did you get done?

04:39.737 --> 04:41.572
It's okay. There's still time.

04:41.656 --> 04:44.409
I already talked to the teacher,
so just finish the exam.

04:44.492 --> 04:45.952
Can you get up?

04:48.621 --> 04:51.541
Mom, I don't feel so good.

04:51.624 --> 04:54.377
It's from staying up all night studying.
Everyone's the same.

04:55.169 --> 04:56.004
Here.

04:57.338 --> 04:58.715
But Mom,

04:59.424 --> 05:01.092
I keep having weird thoughts.

05:02.343 --> 05:04.929
Weird thoughts while studying
mean you're losing focus.

05:06.973 --> 05:08.808
I've brought your medicine.

05:08.891 --> 05:10.184
You'll feel better soon.

05:12.186 --> 05:13.438
Here.

05:18.109 --> 05:18.943
Here.

05:24.991 --> 05:26.576
You're almost there.

05:28.202 --> 05:31.331
You don't want all our hard work
to go to waste, do you?

05:31.998 --> 05:34.292
Hang in there, son. For me?

05:35.209 --> 05:36.961
All right, let's go.

05:58.566 --> 06:02.653
TEACH YOU A LESSON

06:08.451 --> 06:10.495
Attention, students.

06:10.578 --> 06:14.665
There will now be an announcement
of special directives from the ERPB.

06:14.749 --> 06:17.168
All students are to remain on campus

06:17.251 --> 06:20.797
and prepare immediately for urine testing.

06:25.718 --> 06:26.886
SON

06:30.848 --> 06:33.267
Hyeon-min, how did the exam go?

06:34.102 --> 06:35.395
Did you finish?

06:37.855 --> 06:38.898
Why?

06:39.982 --> 06:41.442
What? The ERPB?

06:42.193 --> 06:43.569
They must be crazy.

06:44.070 --> 06:44.904
Okay.

06:44.987 --> 06:47.490
I'll head over to school now.
Call the other moms.

06:47.573 --> 06:48.991
What? The ERPB?

06:50.034 --> 06:52.703
Are they crazy?
The kids have to go to hagwon now.

06:55.832 --> 06:57.375
Where do you think you're going?

06:57.959 --> 06:59.627
Didn't you hear about the test?

06:59.710 --> 07:01.087
We're going to hagwon.

07:01.170 --> 07:02.338
Go after the urine test.

07:02.422 --> 07:04.424
Our moms are coming. You can talk to them.

07:04.507 --> 07:06.884
-What are they doing?
-What's the point of this?

07:06.968 --> 07:09.887
Da-hui, what are you doing?
You'll be late for hagwon. Get going.

07:09.971 --> 07:12.140
-You go ahead.
-What are they doing?

07:12.223 --> 07:14.475
-Go quickly.
-What the hell are they doing?

07:20.565 --> 07:22.984
What do you think you're doing?

07:23.067 --> 07:26.404
-What do you think?
-Hyeon-min's mom, be quiet.

07:27.780 --> 07:30.992
Do you realize
how critical this period is for the kids?

07:31.826 --> 07:35.746
For top students, one point can move them
up or down several university tiers.

07:35.830 --> 07:39.750
There may be no guns, but students
and parents are fighting a war.

07:40.251 --> 07:42.587
So that's why you've put
lives on the line?

07:43.880 --> 07:47.216
You must've heard the rumors.
This test includes a drug screening.

07:47.967 --> 07:51.345
Drugs? Are you suggesting
our kids are on drugs?

07:53.848 --> 07:56.851
Those kids are applying
to SNU Medical School.

07:56.934 --> 07:59.854
-They're not like other kids.
-They all look the same to me.

08:01.814 --> 08:05.568
Have you even thought about what it took
for our kids to get this far?

08:06.694 --> 08:11.282
From birth through preschool,
elementary, middle, and high school,

08:11.365 --> 08:15.036
and now their most crucial year,
they have never wasted a single second.

08:15.119 --> 08:17.830
And what about the moms here?

08:18.331 --> 08:21.083
We sleep an hour less than our kids,
wake up an hour earlier,

08:21.167 --> 08:23.461
send them to hagwon, look for consultants…

08:24.712 --> 08:26.797
If you want them tested,
do it after the CSAT.

08:27.298 --> 08:30.676
Refusing the test will result
in a CSAT penalty. Is that okay?

08:30.760 --> 08:32.261
What do you mean "penalty"?

08:32.345 --> 08:34.514
Are you threatening us
with our kids' lives?

08:34.597 --> 08:36.098
If I were, would you listen?

08:36.182 --> 08:37.850
This is Daechi-dong!

08:37.934 --> 08:39.894
You think you can handle the moms here?

08:39.977 --> 08:40.811
Yes.

08:41.437 --> 08:42.688
The ERPB can handle them.

08:42.772 --> 08:43.814
Then go ahead.

08:43.898 --> 08:45.691
If you want to see people die.

08:45.775 --> 08:48.110
We're doing the test so no one dies.

08:48.194 --> 08:49.695
So we can save even one life

08:50.404 --> 08:51.989
before it's too late.

08:54.200 --> 08:56.160
There's an ERPB-designated hospital.

08:56.244 --> 08:59.288
Take your children there for testing
before school tomorrow.

08:59.372 --> 09:00.665
If you don't,

09:02.208 --> 09:04.293
you won't be able to handle
what comes next.

09:13.177 --> 09:15.346
You're Jung Hyeon-min's mother, right?

09:17.473 --> 09:19.892
Hyeon-min didn't look very well earlier.

09:19.976 --> 09:22.186
Make sure you take him
for the test tomorrow.

09:36.033 --> 09:37.159
By any chance,

09:38.119 --> 09:39.495
do you know who I am?

09:40.454 --> 09:42.957
Well, I've seen you on TV.

09:43.958 --> 09:46.377
You're someone very important.

09:49.171 --> 09:51.757
You hurt your hand
because of the EPRB, right?

09:51.841 --> 09:53.134
Oh, no.

09:53.217 --> 09:55.219
It was my fault.

09:55.303 --> 09:58.681
I'm not trying to blame the ERPB.

09:59.181 --> 10:01.183
I'm trying to help you.

10:02.435 --> 10:03.811
Me? Why?

10:04.812 --> 10:07.523
Providing opportunities
to those who need them

10:08.107 --> 10:09.817
is my job as a politician.

10:11.736 --> 10:13.487
Can I look at your hand again?

10:15.406 --> 10:17.408
It doesn't look like a minor injury.

10:17.491 --> 10:19.243
How about treatment on the outside?

10:22.371 --> 10:26.751
Recently, an armed attack broke out
in a juvenile prison.

10:26.834 --> 10:29.879
A juvenile offender
under the ERPB's supervision

10:29.962 --> 10:32.548
was attacked with a weapon by an inmate.

10:32.632 --> 10:35.217
It could have caused
serious harm or loss of life, but…

10:35.301 --> 10:36.594
-What?
-Oh, nothing.

10:36.677 --> 10:38.179
…the juvenile was unharmed.

10:39.430 --> 10:42.642
However, the inmate who protected him
was the perpetrator of…

10:42.725 --> 10:43.934
-Where is it?
-Well…

10:44.018 --> 10:45.102
That way, sir.

10:45.186 --> 10:46.771
-Lead the way. Hurry up.
-Yes, sir.

10:47.355 --> 10:48.939
They deliberately chose where…

10:49.023 --> 10:52.401
-I wonder where the toilet--
-You're making me more aware of it.

10:52.485 --> 10:54.695
I already saw it all earlier.

10:55.196 --> 10:57.323
Look at you trying so hard.

10:57.406 --> 10:59.659
-Are you okay?
-Of course not.

10:59.742 --> 11:00.993
-That damn photo.
-Come on.

11:01.077 --> 11:02.495
-How did they get it?
-Let's go.

11:02.578 --> 11:04.538
Are the Seungyeon High kids being tested?

11:04.622 --> 11:06.457
Yes, they are.

11:13.881 --> 11:14.757
Need some air?

11:15.341 --> 11:16.217
Let's go outside.

11:24.225 --> 11:25.226
Drink this.

11:28.270 --> 11:30.189
Are you okay? Feeling better?

11:30.272 --> 11:32.149
I'm feeling a bit better.

11:32.233 --> 11:33.192
Good.

11:37.697 --> 11:40.032
REPORT CARDS WERE DISTRIBUTED
TO STUDENTS TODAY

11:41.033 --> 11:42.326
Report cards are out.

11:42.410 --> 11:44.745
-They've also been sent by email. Check.
-Right.

11:57.174 --> 12:00.428
I passed out during the exam
for that subject.

12:03.472 --> 12:04.682
I'm sorry, Mom.

12:12.064 --> 12:13.816
What did I tell you?

12:15.901 --> 12:19.780
Kids like you who can't handle pressure
should at least take your meds properly.

12:21.407 --> 12:23.492
Is it really that hard to take your meds?

12:25.327 --> 12:27.496
Don't you feel sorry for me?

12:28.205 --> 12:31.417
I've had to swallow my pride
in front of the other moms because of you.

12:33.294 --> 12:35.421
Did I ever ask for recognition?

12:37.131 --> 12:39.133
All I'm asking is for you to study.

12:42.052 --> 12:44.138
If you knew how hard I've worked…

12:47.183 --> 12:49.518
For God's sake…

13:20.674 --> 13:24.428
Hyeon-min's goal is SNU Medical School.

13:24.512 --> 13:28.933
I've heard you're a well-known consultant
for medical school admissions.

13:29.642 --> 13:33.270
I'll start by assessing his level.
How advanced is he in his studies?

13:34.396 --> 13:36.398
I've had him study ahead.

13:36.482 --> 13:39.819
He's in first year middle school
but is doing first-year high school math.

13:39.902 --> 13:42.696
He still hasn't finished high school math?

13:44.281 --> 13:46.075
He'll catch up soon.

13:46.575 --> 13:48.953
Our Hyeon-min is top in his grade.

13:49.036 --> 13:52.915
A top student in a provincial school
becomes bottom-tier in Gangnam.

13:53.499 --> 13:55.543
Don't even think about med school.

13:57.127 --> 13:59.547
This isn't exactly the provinces.

13:59.630 --> 14:00.756
We're next to Seoul.

14:00.840 --> 14:02.800
You should meet my son first.
Once you do--

14:02.883 --> 14:04.760
Do you know when moms in Gangnam

14:04.844 --> 14:07.054
start preparing their kids
for SNU's med school?

14:09.014 --> 14:10.266
The moment they're born.

14:11.058 --> 14:13.686
They map out a 20-year plan,
from birth to med school,

14:13.769 --> 14:18.023
and choose preschools, schools, hagwons,
and private tutors accordingly.

14:18.107 --> 14:20.985
These kids have been preparing
for over a decade longer

14:21.068 --> 14:22.945
than those who start in middle school.

14:24.280 --> 14:25.865
By Hyeon-min's age,

14:25.948 --> 14:29.326
he should've already finished studying
the core concepts of the CSAT.

14:29.410 --> 14:32.371
He should be practicing questions
to avoid mistakes on the exam

14:32.454 --> 14:35.749
and working on med school interviews,
essay writing, and English.

14:36.959 --> 14:40.963
Do you understand
just how far behind Hyeon-min is?

14:41.797 --> 14:43.924
Still, he's really…

14:45.593 --> 14:46.635
Kids in Daechi-dong

14:47.928 --> 14:50.514
are tackling questions at this level
right now.

14:53.559 --> 14:54.727
How many of them

14:55.811 --> 14:58.147
do you think Hyeon-min could answer?

15:16.040 --> 15:18.083
DAECHI SKY REAL ESTATE

15:20.044 --> 15:23.339
PRIME LISTING
A HOME THAT SENT KIDS TO SNU MED SCHOOL

15:23.422 --> 15:25.215
GRAND PRIZE IN ENGLISH, JUNG HYEON-MIN

15:26.467 --> 15:29.053
Do you really have to live
in a place like this?

15:30.095 --> 15:32.890
It's within walking distance
of the school and hagwon,

15:32.973 --> 15:34.558
and a bargain for Gangnam.

15:34.642 --> 15:38.354
Besides, the two sons
who grew up here got into SNU.

15:38.854 --> 15:40.314
I even got it with no markup.

15:40.397 --> 15:42.524
I'm not sure about this.

15:42.608 --> 15:45.611
A school is a school.
This area can't be that special.

15:45.694 --> 15:47.237
You have no idea.

15:47.321 --> 15:50.616
Seungyeon High has a med school prep class
just for the top ten students.

15:50.699 --> 15:54.286
If you get into this class,
you're guaranteed SNU med school.

15:54.370 --> 15:56.747
Hyeon-min's goal
is to get into this class.

15:57.957 --> 16:00.793
But still, this place is just…

16:01.502 --> 16:03.212
Aren't you upset?

16:03.712 --> 16:05.631
Didn't your brother go to med school?

16:05.714 --> 16:08.425
Does your family treat you two the same?

16:08.509 --> 16:14.306
But thanks to him, I work at his clinic,
so don't be like that.

16:14.390 --> 16:17.184
That's exactly why
you and I get treated like that

16:17.267 --> 16:19.561
and why Hyeon-min does too.

16:19.645 --> 16:22.189
I'll make sure
Hyeon-min gets into med school

16:22.272 --> 16:23.315
so he's respected.

16:23.399 --> 16:25.567
Who says he's not respected?

16:25.651 --> 16:27.236
That's enough!

16:28.445 --> 16:31.240
Don't be so discouraging.
Just take the door off.

16:31.782 --> 16:33.158
Fine, I will.

16:36.245 --> 16:37.621
I got it.

16:38.122 --> 16:39.581
Okay, hold it.

16:46.630 --> 16:49.383
GOAL
GET INTO SEUNGYEON HIGH!

16:53.012 --> 16:56.682
GOAL
GET INTO SNU MEDICAL SCHOOL!

17:11.655 --> 17:12.489
Here.

17:13.866 --> 17:18.245
I'm not the only one making a fuss.
All the moms around here are like this.

17:19.329 --> 17:20.164
Okay.

17:21.248 --> 17:22.708
Oh, Mom.

17:23.208 --> 17:28.047
What about tutoring?
All the kids seem to have the same tutor.

17:28.839 --> 17:31.091
I'm looking into it, so don't worry.

17:31.633 --> 17:32.551
Keep studying.

17:38.807 --> 17:42.811
Yeong-jun's mom, do you think
you can invite me to the moms' meetings?

17:50.736 --> 17:51.570
Here.

17:52.321 --> 17:53.322
Enjoy.

17:54.698 --> 17:56.450
Forget about all the other moms.

17:56.533 --> 17:58.827
Just stay on Da-hui's mom's good side.

17:59.328 --> 18:00.621
She's the mama pig.

18:00.704 --> 18:01.872
The mama pig?

18:01.955 --> 18:04.666
You know how a sow
has all her piglets following her?

18:04.750 --> 18:07.961
She has all the moms trailing after her,
so she's called the mama pig.

18:11.673 --> 18:14.510
But it's not something just anyone can do.

18:14.593 --> 18:16.970
Information is power for moms here.

18:17.596 --> 18:20.766
And Da-hui's mom has all the connections
with academic coordinators,

18:20.849 --> 18:22.726
admissions consultants,

18:22.810 --> 18:27.189
and even hagwons
with special programs for SNU med school.

18:27.272 --> 18:29.691
You're not a working mom, are you?

18:29.775 --> 18:32.319
No, I'm not. Why?

18:32.402 --> 18:35.322
Working moms, or parents who both work,
can't join this circle.

18:35.405 --> 18:40.202
They just take information and act busy
when it actually matters.

18:40.285 --> 18:44.373
But doctors and professors
get a free pass no matter what.

18:44.957 --> 18:46.208
How come?

18:46.291 --> 18:49.711
You need a strategic student profile
for early admissions.

18:49.795 --> 18:53.674
Hospital volunteer work
and university lab research

18:53.757 --> 18:56.301
make the ultimate student profile.

18:56.385 --> 18:59.138
With Da-hui's mom, it's a done deal.

19:00.973 --> 19:03.433
I'd better stay on her good side.

19:13.485 --> 19:15.279
It's not bedtime yet.

19:15.362 --> 19:16.530
I'm sorry.

19:17.030 --> 19:18.282
I was just so sleepy.

19:18.365 --> 19:20.576
You must be tired. Eat while you study.

19:22.077 --> 19:24.121
Can I have a little more?

19:24.204 --> 19:27.541
A full stomach makes you sleepy.
Your brain only needs glucose.

19:28.292 --> 19:31.712
Just eat this and focus a bit more.

19:31.795 --> 19:32.629
Okay?

19:40.721 --> 19:42.097
Hi, honey.

19:44.141 --> 19:47.352
We're already here,
and you live by yourself.

19:47.436 --> 19:51.231
You can move to a cheaper studio
or move in with your mother.

19:52.900 --> 19:55.068
It's all for Hyeon-min!

20:00.449 --> 20:02.159
Once he succeeds,

20:02.743 --> 20:04.161
it will all be worth it.

20:19.968 --> 20:21.762
I didn't want to come empty-handed.

20:22.262 --> 20:23.972
I hope you like it.

20:25.724 --> 20:27.226
You didn't have to.

20:32.856 --> 20:35.108
I came to see you because--

20:35.192 --> 20:37.653
Every mom comes to see me
for the same reason.

20:37.736 --> 20:39.613
And I already heard from Yeong-jun's mom.

20:40.489 --> 20:43.992
Just come to a few of our meetings
and see how it goes.

20:46.245 --> 20:47.079
Okay.

20:47.579 --> 20:49.164
Was it? Was it okay?

20:50.123 --> 20:51.166
What would you like?

20:51.250 --> 20:53.460
-I'll have an iced latte.
-A latte.

20:53.543 --> 20:55.921
-Double shot, please.
-Double shot? Okay.

20:56.004 --> 20:57.547
DOUBLE SHOT

20:58.382 --> 21:01.176
-This is already too much.
-This is only the start, okay?

21:02.052 --> 21:02.970
Here you go.

21:03.053 --> 21:05.013
Here's your latte.

21:05.097 --> 21:07.849
-She's a natural.
-Yeah, you're right. It's Da-hui.

21:07.933 --> 21:09.518
That's why she's at that level.

21:09.601 --> 21:12.229
For math, Ms. Jung Da-eun is the best.

21:13.355 --> 21:15.148
She gets kids into SNU med school.

21:15.232 --> 21:16.483
MATH
JUNG DA-EUN

21:16.566 --> 21:18.819
One downside is
that her academic background isn't great.

21:25.742 --> 21:27.661
ENGLISH
OH BO-HYEON

21:31.206 --> 21:34.334
It's easier if you start
by calculating 6 choose 2.

21:34.835 --> 21:35.961
What's 6 choose 2?

21:36.044 --> 21:38.213
Then what's 15 times 6?

21:38.297 --> 21:39.965
-90.
-That's correct.

21:40.048 --> 21:43.427
90 is correct. Try solving this one
and see if you understand.

21:43.510 --> 21:45.220
REPORT CARD
YEAR 1, SEMESTER 1, 2024

22:03.572 --> 22:04.906
Don't worry.

22:04.990 --> 22:07.367
They say grades
depend on how much parents put in.

22:07.451 --> 22:08.285
Go on.

22:14.541 --> 22:17.252
For God's sake.

22:22.257 --> 22:24.259
It turns out these plates come as a set.

22:24.343 --> 22:27.346
If I'd known, I would've brought
the whole set last time.

22:28.638 --> 22:29.890
You didn't have to.

22:31.600 --> 22:33.018
I heard about Hyeon-min.

22:33.101 --> 22:35.812
He didn't get into
the med school prep class again, right?

22:35.896 --> 22:42.361
I got him the tutor you recommended,
and he goes to the same hagwon as Da-hui,

22:42.444 --> 22:44.613
so I don't know what the problem is.

22:44.696 --> 22:48.241
Sitting at a desk for hours
doesn't guarantee good grades.

22:48.325 --> 22:50.160
Even with the same study time,

22:50.243 --> 22:54.623
some kids take in 100%,
while others only take in 50%.

22:55.123 --> 22:56.958
That's the difference in focus.

22:58.085 --> 23:00.504
Is there a tutor for that too?

23:03.215 --> 23:06.635
There are things a teacher can help with
and things they can't.

23:09.763 --> 23:10.806
Hold on.

23:22.651 --> 23:25.070
Here, try giving him this.

23:25.570 --> 23:27.906
His focus will improve dramatically.

23:27.989 --> 23:31.618
Da-hui and her older brother took it,
and their grades went up.

23:55.725 --> 23:56.601
Hyeon-min.

23:59.354 --> 24:03.733
I went through a lot to get this for you
so you can study better.

24:04.359 --> 24:07.821
I know you'd do so well
if you really got your head in the game.

24:07.904 --> 24:09.322
I hear this stuff is amazing.

24:09.406 --> 24:12.409
You'll focus better
and be less nervous during exams.

24:13.326 --> 24:15.745
All the kids around here take it.

24:24.796 --> 24:25.630
Drink this.

24:29.718 --> 24:31.928
This is an illegal drug.

24:33.763 --> 24:35.891
You all look like you already knew.

24:36.933 --> 24:39.853
It's an unapproved ADHD medication
in Korea.

24:39.936 --> 24:43.607
Yet it has already been circulating
discreetly among mothers

24:43.690 --> 24:44.983
because it's effective.

24:45.484 --> 24:46.401
I'm sure you know.

24:48.820 --> 24:52.449
In the urine tests,
the children tested positive

24:52.532 --> 24:54.367
for methylphenidate and atomoxetine.

24:54.451 --> 24:58.455
These two drugs
are only for high-risk patients

24:58.538 --> 25:00.790
and are very rarely prescribed together.

25:00.874 --> 25:03.210
In particular,
methylphenidate is classified

25:03.293 --> 25:06.254
as a controlled psychotropic substance

25:06.338 --> 25:08.423
under the Narcotics Control Act in Korea.

25:09.007 --> 25:12.344
This means taking it
without a prescription is illegal.

25:14.179 --> 25:18.683
It violates the Narcotics Control Act
and the Pharmaceutical Affairs Act,

25:18.767 --> 25:20.602
making it a criminal offense.

25:21.228 --> 25:22.062
It'll be okay.

25:22.145 --> 25:23.939
Everyone here will be subject

25:24.606 --> 25:26.525
to police questioning.

25:29.569 --> 25:30.654
Inspector.

25:30.737 --> 25:31.571
Yes?

25:31.655 --> 25:34.574
The test results for Jung Hyeon-min
are concerning.

25:35.909 --> 25:37.244
Hyeon-min's mom.

25:38.411 --> 25:40.497
Where did Hyeon-min's mother go?

25:40.580 --> 25:44.167
-Hyeon-min's mom? Where did she go?
-I think she went out that way.

25:44.251 --> 25:45.293
Maybe to the bathroom?

25:45.377 --> 25:47.379
I heard Hyeon-min's grades have gone up.

25:49.089 --> 25:51.508
He must have been really determined.

25:51.591 --> 25:52.884
He's completely changed.

25:52.968 --> 25:55.053
He seems to have gotten mentally stronger.

25:55.136 --> 25:57.806
I think he'll make it
into the med school prep class soon.

25:58.473 --> 26:00.934
Still, the competition is really intense.

26:01.434 --> 26:06.147
Do you know of any medicine
that's better than the one you gave me?

26:06.231 --> 26:07.190
Well,

26:07.274 --> 26:11.027
I could find out if I looked into it,
but that one should be enough.

26:11.945 --> 26:12.862
I see.

26:15.407 --> 26:19.202
My child's grades improved
after taking ADHD medication.

26:19.286 --> 26:23.707
I'm looking for something more effective.
If anyone knows, please help.

26:24.374 --> 26:26.918
Could you tell me what medication he took
that improved his grades?

26:27.002 --> 26:29.170
They're no help at all.

26:33.883 --> 26:36.511
I have the meds
last year's top med school entrant took.

26:36.595 --> 26:37.762
Do you want it?

27:06.333 --> 27:08.043
You're from the forum, right?

27:08.877 --> 27:09.711
Yes.

27:35.070 --> 27:38.198
TIER 1

27:45.747 --> 27:48.083
Well done, my son.

27:49.209 --> 27:51.419
Can you get
into the med school prep class now?

27:51.503 --> 27:54.798
Yes, they told me
to join the class tomorrow.

27:57.092 --> 27:57.926
That's great.

28:00.929 --> 28:01.888
Well done.

28:12.190 --> 28:13.692
JUNG HYEON-MIN'S MOTHER

28:13.775 --> 28:15.777
She's still not picking up.

28:15.860 --> 28:18.947
They found another substance
in Hyeon-min's system besides ADHD meds.

28:19.030 --> 28:20.365
It's in the Heart Pills too.

28:20.448 --> 28:21.408
What?

28:23.410 --> 28:25.495
The amount is almost a lethal dose.

28:26.496 --> 28:29.082
If he keeps taking it
or increases the dose,

28:29.165 --> 28:30.709
couldn't it be life-threatening?

28:30.792 --> 28:33.128
-That's right.
-"That's right"? It's not…

28:33.628 --> 28:35.046
Are you crawling or what?

28:35.547 --> 28:36.631
I'm on it, kid!

28:44.931 --> 28:46.099
Hyeon-min.

28:46.933 --> 28:48.017
It's not your fault.

28:49.269 --> 28:50.603
You just got unlucky.

28:51.229 --> 28:53.565
Early admission is out,
but you still have the CSAT.

28:53.648 --> 28:56.025
If you do well,
you can still get into med school.

28:59.487 --> 29:01.823
You can pull yourself together
and do this, right?

29:03.283 --> 29:06.828
I'll get you excused for field study,
so don't go to school.

29:06.911 --> 29:09.247
Just study at home until the CSAT.

29:09.330 --> 29:10.331
Okay?

29:15.462 --> 29:16.546
Mom.

29:18.256 --> 29:19.883
Can you get me the meds?

29:21.342 --> 29:22.177
Yes.

29:22.677 --> 29:24.179
Let's take the meds and study.

29:43.448 --> 29:44.449
Hyeon-min.

29:45.867 --> 29:46.701
Jung Hyeon-min!

29:51.748 --> 29:53.208
Hyeon-min, are you in there?

29:55.835 --> 29:57.629
HIGH SCHOOL SENIOR INSIDE
DO NOT RING!

30:07.472 --> 30:08.723
Oh no.

30:15.730 --> 30:17.357
They won't let me in.

30:17.440 --> 30:18.983
All right, sir.

30:20.860 --> 30:22.946
-What did he say?
-They won't let him in.

30:24.823 --> 30:26.658
However I see it, it seems dangerous.

30:26.741 --> 30:28.868
You're not actually going to jump,
are you?

30:28.952 --> 30:31.204
-The kid might die at this rate.
-What?

30:35.667 --> 30:37.836
Oh my God, why are you up there?

30:38.503 --> 30:39.838
Hold that tight, okay?

30:41.381 --> 30:42.382
Oh my God!

30:44.634 --> 30:45.468
Wait.

31:07.156 --> 31:09.784
Wait, Hyeon-min! The ERPB is here.

31:22.088 --> 31:23.506
Inspector Im Han-rim!

31:23.590 --> 31:25.592
Are you all right?

31:26.634 --> 31:28.219
-What the…
-Hyeon-min!

31:28.303 --> 31:29.679
-Let go.
-No.

31:29.762 --> 31:32.181
-Give me the pills!
-No! Let go!

31:32.682 --> 31:34.225
No!

31:34.309 --> 31:36.227
-Take Hyeon-min to the hospital.
-Okay.

31:37.562 --> 31:39.522
No, you can't!

31:39.606 --> 31:41.482
-Let go. Hyeon-min!
-Come on!

31:42.191 --> 31:43.735
Let me go. Hyeon-min!

31:43.818 --> 31:45.612
Let me go. Hyeon-min!

31:48.615 --> 31:50.700
Why are you taking Hyeon-min?

31:52.702 --> 31:55.246
Ma'am, do you know
what kind of medication this is?

31:56.998 --> 31:59.334
Some students call it
a pill that keeps them awake,

31:59.417 --> 32:00.960
helps them focus,

32:01.044 --> 32:03.630
treats ADHD, boosts their grades,

32:03.713 --> 32:05.465
and gets them into med school.

32:05.548 --> 32:06.966
But we call it

32:07.467 --> 32:09.135
a pill that kills people.

32:10.803 --> 32:12.597
We call it an illicit drug.

32:15.558 --> 32:17.894
-What do you mean "illicit drug"?
-Didn't you know?

32:19.354 --> 32:20.563
No.

32:21.147 --> 32:24.067
I just gave it to him
because I heard it helps with focus.

32:24.150 --> 32:25.318
Did you really not know?

32:25.401 --> 32:27.111
How could I have?

32:27.195 --> 32:29.614
This is the first time
I'm hearing that it's bad!

32:29.697 --> 32:31.449
Did you really not know?

32:32.325 --> 32:34.452
Did you really not see
the changes in Hyeon-min…

32:36.871 --> 32:38.414
after he started taking it?

32:47.340 --> 32:48.216
Hyeon-min.

32:54.973 --> 32:56.641
Here, I got you. Oh my!

32:59.268 --> 33:00.895
I WANT TO DIE

33:00.979 --> 33:03.356
You knew this drug

33:03.898 --> 33:05.608
was ruining Hyeon-min.

33:25.086 --> 33:26.629
What were you thinking?

33:26.713 --> 33:28.548
As long as he could get into med school,

33:29.549 --> 33:32.260
you thought it was okay
to give him drugs like this?

33:33.720 --> 33:36.097
I was only going to give it to him
until the CSAT.

33:36.180 --> 33:38.975
Something could go wrong
with him before then.

33:39.058 --> 33:40.893
Is med school worth more than your son?

33:46.649 --> 33:48.443
I guess it is.

33:49.152 --> 33:50.820
He's almost there.

33:51.320 --> 33:54.365
Every second counts.
There's no time for this!

33:54.449 --> 33:56.617
Hyeon-min needs to study!

33:57.201 --> 33:58.286
From this moment on,

33:58.369 --> 34:01.080
you are not allowed
to leave this apartment.

34:01.164 --> 34:02.290
Why not?

34:02.373 --> 34:03.624
This is my home!

34:03.708 --> 34:05.376
This is to protect Hyeon-min.

34:05.460 --> 34:09.255
The ERPB will now separate
the child abuser from the victim.

34:09.338 --> 34:11.340
What do you mean "child abuse"?

34:11.424 --> 34:13.593
I'm his mother!

34:13.676 --> 34:16.804
I told you this is the most important time
of his life!

34:17.722 --> 34:21.517
Will you take responsibility
if he misses out on med school?

34:28.191 --> 34:30.276
If you want med school that badly,

34:32.153 --> 34:33.446
go yourself.

34:46.793 --> 34:48.294
Hyeon-min, are you okay?

34:50.671 --> 34:52.006
Oh my God, no!

34:54.634 --> 34:56.135
What are you doing?

34:57.595 --> 34:58.429
It's okay.

34:58.930 --> 34:59.764
Hyeon-min.

35:02.475 --> 35:05.228
Why put your hand there
when you have zero pain tolerance?

35:06.437 --> 35:09.065
It's better my hand gets hurt
than his head.

35:13.027 --> 35:15.404
Do you have a fever?
You're like a different person.

35:18.741 --> 35:20.076
Looking at Hyeon-min

35:20.576 --> 35:22.370
reminds me of my younger self.

35:22.954 --> 35:24.872
My mom tried to send me to med school too.

35:24.956 --> 35:26.582
So why didn't you go?

35:27.166 --> 35:29.127
Because it wasn't fun at all.

35:38.719 --> 35:40.680
CSAT PREP
SAMPLE QUESTIONS

35:43.057 --> 35:44.684
What are you trying to pull here?

35:44.767 --> 35:46.102
I told you.

35:46.853 --> 35:48.729
If you want med school, go yourself.

35:48.813 --> 35:51.732
Do you know why I want Hyeon-min
to go to med school?

35:52.817 --> 35:55.945
I have no connections.
Nothing to leave him either.

35:56.779 --> 35:59.740
When kids have to compete,
they end up resenting their parents.

35:59.824 --> 36:03.119
That's why you should study
and go to med school yourself.

36:03.202 --> 36:05.454
Then you can be his connection.

36:06.122 --> 36:07.790
Why do you want him to be self-made?

36:07.874 --> 36:09.709
He'd prefer well-off parents.

36:09.792 --> 36:12.044
How am I supposed to go to med school
at my age?

36:13.087 --> 36:15.089
I think you could if you stuck to this.

36:16.549 --> 36:17.425
These are

36:18.926 --> 36:23.014
the study and meal plans you made
for Hyeon-min.

36:23.598 --> 36:25.099
You planned it really well.

36:25.600 --> 36:27.351
If you stick to this,

36:27.852 --> 36:29.645
you could easily get into med school.

36:33.232 --> 36:34.108
Study.

36:34.692 --> 36:38.446
Once your mock exam scores
clear the med school cutoff,

36:38.529 --> 36:40.615
I'll let you see Hyeon-min.

36:42.366 --> 36:43.451
For God's sake!

36:44.493 --> 36:46.120
17:30. Instead of going to hagwon,

36:46.204 --> 36:49.540
work through the past CSAT English paper
at least three times.

36:52.460 --> 36:55.046
If you get even one question wrong,
start over.

37:02.303 --> 37:04.472
It's not time to eat yet.

37:04.972 --> 37:07.099
Nutritional support for brain function.

37:07.183 --> 37:08.142
What's this?

37:08.226 --> 37:09.769
It's your dinner.

37:10.269 --> 37:11.604
Being full makes you sleepy.

37:12.230 --> 37:15.566
By the way,
I'm just following the meal plan.

37:20.613 --> 37:21.614
No? I'll take them.

37:22.490 --> 37:23.324
I'll eat them.

37:29.455 --> 37:33.000
After watching online lectures
and completing an error log,

37:33.084 --> 37:34.085
sleep at 1:00 a.m.

37:39.548 --> 37:40.716
It's time to wake up.

37:43.970 --> 37:45.346
Let me sleep a little longer.

37:45.429 --> 37:48.057
Sleep four hours, you pass.
Sleep five, you fail!

37:48.140 --> 37:49.058
Oh man.

37:49.141 --> 37:50.017
So loud.

37:51.227 --> 37:52.228
Oh my goodness!

37:52.812 --> 37:54.230
What are you doing?

37:55.231 --> 37:57.858
I'm getting rid of this mattress
as it's distracting.

37:57.942 --> 38:00.111
Isn't that why you took this door off?

38:00.611 --> 38:01.946
Are you insane?

38:02.029 --> 38:05.574
Insane? Can't you see
that I'm sacrificing myself for you?

38:05.658 --> 38:07.618
More like fooling around.

38:08.577 --> 38:10.037
Does this look like a joke?

38:10.538 --> 38:14.333
Do you think I'd make you suffer the same,
and then one day say,

38:14.417 --> 38:19.338
"That's enough. Let's go see Hyeon-min
since you've learned your lesson"?

38:22.383 --> 38:24.135
That will never

38:25.052 --> 38:26.846
ever happen.

38:29.265 --> 38:33.019
There's only one way
you can leave this place.

38:34.562 --> 38:36.814
By getting into med school.

38:57.168 --> 38:59.503
You're up. Are you feeling okay?

39:01.630 --> 39:02.840
I'm sorry.

39:05.301 --> 39:06.927
You hurt your hand because of me.

39:08.804 --> 39:09.638
It's fine.

39:14.352 --> 39:15.227
What is it?

39:17.146 --> 39:17.980
Hey.

39:19.690 --> 39:21.525
Can you get me those pills?

39:22.401 --> 39:23.361
No.

39:24.195 --> 39:25.237
They're harmful.

39:26.906 --> 39:28.449
Harmful?

39:28.532 --> 39:29.992
It's an illegal drug.

39:35.414 --> 39:36.415
Can I just have one?

39:36.499 --> 39:37.833
-No.
-I swear it's the last.

39:37.917 --> 39:40.544
-No, Hyeon-min.
-I feel like I'll die without it!

39:40.628 --> 39:41.921
No. I said no!

39:42.421 --> 39:44.465
Do you think you can control it?

39:45.049 --> 39:48.177
Everyone says "just one" at first.
Then they say "just one more."

39:48.260 --> 39:50.304
That's how you ruin yourself.

39:50.805 --> 39:51.889
Your body,

39:51.972 --> 39:53.182
your mind,

39:54.350 --> 39:55.601
and even your life.

39:59.772 --> 40:02.525
If you don't want to die,
hold out until the end.

40:20.292 --> 40:21.585
You failed.

40:31.470 --> 40:32.388
Fail.

40:33.222 --> 40:34.306
You improved a little.

40:36.392 --> 40:37.435
Fail.

41:12.011 --> 41:14.763
STUDY SCHEDULE
JUST ONE MORE YEAR. YOU CAN DO THIS, SON

41:14.847 --> 41:17.683
GOAL
GET INTO SNU MEDICAL SCHOOL!

41:21.145 --> 41:23.230
I WANT TO DIE

41:36.744 --> 41:38.204
I wanted to die.

41:39.330 --> 41:41.415
I felt like the hell I was in
would never end

41:41.916 --> 41:44.126
unless I got into med school.

41:50.508 --> 41:53.802
Every time I felt like I wanted to die,
I took the pills.

41:58.682 --> 41:59.600
Mom.

42:00.643 --> 42:03.521
Can I skip hagwon today?

42:03.604 --> 42:05.481
Why? What's wrong now?

42:05.564 --> 42:08.108
Those who hold out now
will be smiling later.

42:08.609 --> 42:09.777
You can do it, right?

42:50.568 --> 42:52.403
Why did you skip hagwon?

42:56.407 --> 42:57.449
I'm sorry.

43:21.849 --> 43:23.642
When I took the pills Mom got me,

43:23.726 --> 43:26.228
I didn't want to die anymore.

43:28.022 --> 43:29.732
But only for a moment.

43:30.399 --> 43:33.694
Soon after,
I felt like I wanted to die again.

43:34.194 --> 43:37.031
Can you get me stronger pills?

43:39.700 --> 43:40.576
Okay.

43:42.077 --> 43:44.705
I took those pills
because I didn't want to die.

43:45.331 --> 43:47.791
Because I wanted to live.

43:50.753 --> 43:52.546
It's possible to live without them.

43:53.672 --> 43:56.717
Let's quit the pills
and anything that makes you feel suicidal.

43:57.843 --> 44:00.846
If it's studying, then quit studying.

44:01.972 --> 44:04.391
If it's med school,
then quit trying for it.

44:05.893 --> 44:07.144
And if it's your mom,

44:07.686 --> 44:08.979
quit your mom too.

44:15.903 --> 44:17.404
How would I quit my mom?

44:23.577 --> 44:25.704
That was a bit too much, wasn't it?

44:27.873 --> 44:28.707
Sorry.

44:44.973 --> 44:45.849
It's my birthday.

44:46.850 --> 44:47.976
Do you know when it is?

44:52.940 --> 44:54.191
Let me out.

44:54.775 --> 44:56.318
It's too hard. I can't go on.

44:56.402 --> 44:58.779
So when it's too hard,
you just get to quit?

44:59.571 --> 45:01.073
You didn't let Hyeon-min do that.

45:01.156 --> 45:04.702
Do you really think
I was trying to kill my son?

45:04.785 --> 45:08.163
I sold a perfectly good home
and moved into this dump.

45:08.247 --> 45:11.834
I acted like a servant
to the moms just to get information.

45:11.917 --> 45:14.169
I got up early every morning
to make breakfast.

45:14.920 --> 45:17.047
I've never lived a day for myself.

45:17.631 --> 45:20.843
I couldn't even have a hobby
because I had to pay his hagwon fees.

45:20.926 --> 45:25.097
I did all this and sacrificed myself
so Hyeon-min could succeed.

45:27.307 --> 45:30.602
You didn't sacrifice yourself
for Hyeon-min.

45:31.103 --> 45:32.813
Hyeon-min…

45:35.816 --> 45:37.985
sacrificed himself for you.

45:46.910 --> 45:48.203
DRAW YOUR DREAM JOB

45:50.497 --> 45:52.124
NAME: JUNG HYEON-MIN
DREAM: DOCTOR

45:55.461 --> 45:58.464
Mommy would be so happy
if you became a doctor.

45:58.547 --> 46:01.383
-Really?
-Yes, of course.

46:01.467 --> 46:03.927
WHAT WILL YOU BE IN THE FUTURE?

46:04.511 --> 46:06.722
You should become a doctor, of course,

46:06.805 --> 46:08.807
and take care of me whenever I'm sick.

46:11.935 --> 46:13.270
"Doctor."

46:13.979 --> 46:15.689
You're a good boy.

46:16.190 --> 46:17.483
You always listen to me.

46:18.066 --> 46:18.984
Yeah.

46:23.030 --> 46:24.948
Don't you feel bad for me and your dad?

46:25.866 --> 46:27.785
Why do you think we live like this?

46:27.868 --> 46:30.037
We're sacrificing for you.

46:30.704 --> 46:33.624
I'm sacrificing myself for you!

46:37.336 --> 46:38.587
Jung Hyeon-min!

46:39.087 --> 46:41.465
Do you think I enjoy this?

46:41.548 --> 46:43.467
I'm putting up with it for you.

46:43.550 --> 46:45.177
Mom, I'm sorry.

46:45.260 --> 46:48.430
If it weren't for you,
I could live a happy life.

46:48.514 --> 46:50.390
I'm sacrificing myself for you!

46:58.065 --> 47:00.526
Ever since I was little,
Mom has always told me

47:01.026 --> 47:02.736
that I have to become a doctor.

47:05.072 --> 47:08.116
So I naturally thought
I should become one.

47:13.205 --> 47:14.414
Sounds stupid, right?

47:19.336 --> 47:21.588
You said you did well in school, right?

47:22.464 --> 47:23.841
Nah, not really.

47:24.341 --> 47:27.177
Please tell me
what I'm supposed to do first.

47:30.681 --> 47:31.598
First,

47:32.099 --> 47:34.142
think about what you like the most.

47:35.435 --> 47:38.981
I'm happiest
when I do what I enjoy the most.

47:40.774 --> 47:44.111
I can name hundreds of things
my mom likes.

47:45.404 --> 47:47.489
But I can't think
of a single thing I like.

47:49.116 --> 47:50.450
What do I like?

47:54.830 --> 47:58.041
It's not too late to think about it.
Let's figure it out together.

47:58.667 --> 48:00.043
You too, Inspector Im.

48:03.297 --> 48:04.298
Just come on.

48:04.798 --> 48:06.008
Give me a second.

48:06.091 --> 48:08.302
I'm here for the books I asked for.

48:08.385 --> 48:09.344
Oh, yes.

48:09.428 --> 48:11.054
Pediatric center?

48:18.729 --> 48:19.938
Here, read these.

48:20.022 --> 48:21.148
KANG WON-MI THE JUDO GIRL

48:21.231 --> 48:22.983
-You know how old he is, right?
-Yeah.

48:23.817 --> 48:25.235
Here, you can read this.

48:25.736 --> 48:26.778
This is for you.

48:27.279 --> 48:29.197
-Come on.
-This is a children's book.

48:30.115 --> 48:31.366
You want me to read this?

48:31.450 --> 48:32.618
-Yeah.
-Me? It's for me?

48:32.701 --> 48:34.786
HAMSTER YAMMA WHO BECAME A YOUTUBER

48:40.918 --> 48:42.628
CHOI THE FIREFIGHTER CAT

49:29.257 --> 49:30.300
Get ready.

49:30.384 --> 49:31.718
We're going out.

49:45.107 --> 49:46.274
Hyeon-min.

49:48.986 --> 49:49.903
Are you okay?

49:49.987 --> 49:50.862
Yeah.

49:50.946 --> 49:52.239
Are you sure you're okay?

49:52.322 --> 49:53.991
I'm doing better.

49:57.536 --> 49:58.578
I'm glad to hear that.

50:01.373 --> 50:04.543
How are your studies?
You have been studying, right?

50:08.880 --> 50:11.216
I don't mean to pressure you,

50:11.299 --> 50:13.760
but the CSAT is coming up,
and I'm worried.

50:15.095 --> 50:16.513
You understand, don't you?

50:20.809 --> 50:22.102
Are you comfortable here?

50:22.602 --> 50:24.229
Is the food okay?

50:49.921 --> 50:50.756
Mom.

50:51.923 --> 50:52.924
Yeah?

50:54.801 --> 50:56.428
I have something to tell you.

50:57.179 --> 50:59.097
You do? What is it?

51:00.640 --> 51:02.142
I'm not going to med school.

51:02.768 --> 51:04.144
And I'm not taking the CSAT.

51:06.313 --> 51:07.230
What?

51:07.731 --> 51:09.399
I'll keep studying though.

51:09.900 --> 51:12.277
And I'll take the CSAT next year.

51:14.237 --> 51:16.406
But not this year.

51:16.907 --> 51:19.159
I don't want to live like this,

51:20.535 --> 51:22.829
aimless and doing what I'm told.

51:23.413 --> 51:24.790
I have no idea

51:25.582 --> 51:28.168
what you're talking about right now.

51:28.752 --> 51:29.586
Mom.

51:34.841 --> 51:36.593
Even if I don't take the CSAT

51:37.761 --> 51:39.096
or go to med school…

51:43.100 --> 51:44.684
I'm still your son.

51:46.019 --> 51:46.978
What are you--

51:47.062 --> 51:49.815
No matter what I decide,
please support me, Mom.

51:52.067 --> 51:53.485
No, Hyeon-min.

51:54.653 --> 51:56.446
You have to take the CSAT.

51:56.947 --> 51:58.490
You need to go to med school!

52:08.125 --> 52:09.668
I'm heading to my treatment now.

52:12.254 --> 52:13.922
No, Hyeon-min!

52:14.840 --> 52:15.757
No.

52:18.260 --> 52:20.595
I hope you stop suffering because of me

52:20.679 --> 52:23.390
and live your own life.

53:17.235 --> 53:20.989
In a recent inspection of all elementary,
middle, and high schools,

53:21.072 --> 53:25.410
many students tested positive
for ingredients from overseas ADHD drugs

53:25.493 --> 53:28.663
that are not approved domestically.

53:28.747 --> 53:29.998
In several cases,

53:30.081 --> 53:33.585
we detected a substance known
among parents and students as a study aid.

53:35.837 --> 53:36.796
This drug,

53:36.880 --> 53:40.759
also known as "Heart Pills,"

53:40.842 --> 53:43.303
contains designer drug components.

53:44.137 --> 53:47.057
In the future, the ERPB
will conduct screenings before the CSAT,

53:47.140 --> 53:51.436
and any student who tests positive
for illegal drugs

53:51.519 --> 53:52.896
will be disqualified.

54:04.366 --> 54:06.243
Are there this many types of drugs?

54:06.326 --> 54:09.246
They look different
but have similar ingredients.

54:09.955 --> 54:12.415
These Full Moon Pills
were popular about ten years ago,

54:12.499 --> 54:14.918
and these Snowman Pills
were popular five years ago.

54:15.001 --> 54:18.129
And these letters in the middle
were engraved by the dealers.

54:18.213 --> 54:21.174
They're like a trademark for a product.

54:22.342 --> 54:25.345
-These were popular two years ago--
-Excuse me.

54:28.181 --> 54:29.891
Could I take a quick look at this?

54:43.863 --> 54:46.074
We're fucked, damn it!

54:47.409 --> 54:48.827
What are we going to do now?

54:48.910 --> 54:52.664
Those fucking ERPB assholes
blocked everything.

54:57.627 --> 54:58.628
Isn't it obvious?

54:58.712 --> 55:01.256
The ERPB just needs to disappear,
doesn't it?

55:03.091 --> 55:05.218
WHAT SHOULD I DO… ABOUT GYU-CHEOL?

55:16.980 --> 55:21.609
WILL I EVER BE ABLE TO… FORGIVE GYU-CHEOL?

55:25.572 --> 55:27.490
CRACKDOWN ON GEN Z-TARGETED DESIGNER DRUGS

55:35.165 --> 55:37.917
Gyu-cheol, let's say

55:38.418 --> 55:42.339
your parole hearing goes well
and you're released back into society.

55:43.214 --> 55:45.008
What would you want to do most?

55:49.054 --> 55:50.055
I'm not sure.

55:50.764 --> 55:52.807
I don't even dare hope for it.

55:54.351 --> 55:57.896
But if it were possible…

56:00.940 --> 56:03.151
I'd want to go back to school.

56:05.570 --> 56:08.281
WILL I EVER BE ABLE TO… FORGIVE GYU-CHEOL?

56:08.365 --> 56:09.657
Based on witness statements

56:09.741 --> 56:14.871
that the defendant, Cho Gyu-cheol,
showed ongoing hostility toward Ms. Choi,

56:14.954 --> 56:19.042
we seek ten years' imprisonment
for premeditated retaliatory murder.

56:20.001 --> 56:21.252
It is clear

56:21.336 --> 56:23.713
Cho Gyu-cheol was changing
under Ms. Choi's guidance.

56:24.381 --> 56:27.550
This was nothing more
than a deeply unfortunate accident.

56:43.525 --> 56:44.484
Get on now.

57:59.934 --> 58:02.896
Subtitle translation by: Lisa Kim
